      "problem": "Find the inverse of the function $f(x)=4x+3b$, where $b$ is a constant.",
      "worked_solution": "To find the inverse of a function, we follow these steps:\n\n**Step 1:** Replace $f(x)$ with $y$:\n\n$$\ny=4x+3b\n$$\n\n**Step 2:** Swap $x$ and $y$:\n\n$$\nx=4y+3b\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Solve for $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =4y+3b \\\\ x-3b & =4y \\\\ \\frac{x-3b}{4} & =y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 4:** Replace $y$ with ${f}^{-1}(x)$:\n\n$$\n{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{x-3b}{4}\n$$",
